# Adding a new MF remote

Do **not** hand-copy vite configs, shell remotes, router routes, sider links, or Tailwind `@source` lines.

## Nx generator (preferred)

```bash
nx g @react-mfe/workspace-plugin:remote orders --port=5104 --no-interactive
# optional: --title=Orders --blurb="Order list remote"
# port omitted → next free port from remotes.json
```

Or:

```bash
bun run create-remote --name=orders --port=5104
```

## What that updates

| Piece | Where | Manual? |
| ----- | ----- | ------- |
| Registry | `packages/mf-config/remotes.json` | generator |
| App scaffold | `apps/<name>/` | generator |
| Shell MF / routes / sider / home | read `REMOTES` | auto |
| `bun run dev` | `scripts/dev-all.mjs` | auto |
| Tailwind scan | `apps/*/src` glob | auto |

Plugin lives at `tools/workspace-plugin` (`remote` generator).

## After create

1. Implement UI in `apps/<name>/src/App.tsx` (expose stays `./App`).
2. `bun run dev`.

## Removing a remote

```bash
bun run delete-remote --name promotions
bun run delete-remote --name cart --force   # orphan folder after Vite lock
```

Stop `bun run dev` first on Windows (`EACCES` / `EBUSY`).
